gianna runs jumps flies and whirls  through the world or the imaginary world  in the computer game jana sisters  twisted dreams  just like a quarter of a century ago  gianna has to fight through increasingly  difficult levels collecting diamonds and  battling evil monsters to save her  sister  the original version of this game now  belongs to the software studio black  forest games from offenborg  this new edition of giana sisters is  their first product  and it's already sold more than a  million copies  you see more and more old titles being  pulled out reworked and given a new look  and feel  developers have retained janna's  trademark double personality at the push  of a button she morphs from a lovable  girl into an alter ego with a punk look  and feel  that changes her abilities and her  surroundings  stefan schmitz was responsible for  adapting the old game into its modern  form he designed the individual levels  two things were really important for us  with john a sister's twisted dreams  first we wanted to stay true to the  original and the feelings it evoked  and we also wanted to use it to realize  our own interests and preferences  the original version of the game hit the  market in 1987.  but the german programmers were accused  by japanese company nintendo of  copyright infringement of its game super  mario brothers  the great gianna sisters was then taken  off the market  but pirated copies continued to sell  making the game something of a cult  favorite  original versions can be bought on the  internet for up to three and a half  thousand  euros it's no coincidence that the  offenburg studio hit upon jana sisters  for its first project  one of the programmers of the original  was a co-founder of black forest games  predecessor  back then the company had 70 employees  and plenty of success  with games such as airline tycoon and  desperados  but two years ago investors pulled out  and the firm went bust  a core team then acquired the rights to  jana sisters and founded black forest  games  the industry moves and changes so fast  that we were always aware we were taking  a big risk  but we also realized that this is what  we really want to do  the founders of the giana project began  a crowdfunding campaign on the internet  platform kickstarter and more than six  thousand private individuals and fans  invested some 135 000 euros in the game  for a studio like ours it's an  story the financing  and  important  maybe that was the case in the beginning  but now the funds you can get on  kickstarter have also dwindled  but it was great to test the interest in  such a computer game early on before  it's been developed it has the test  windows  and cooks so you can quickly see whether  your target audience is interested  in  some of the original staff were rehired  many could have made big money working  outside the computer games industry but  the programmers driven by their passion  stayed on and designed the game within  12 months  even chris hulsbeck the composer of the  original game is excited about his role  first of all i think it's great that i  could be part of this project because  the classic janus is this game was a  milestone of my career  are nine nationalities among the black  forest games employees many have become  good friends and they often cook  together at lunchtime  when we release jhana sisters the  company grew as  black forest games will take the  kickstarter route again on their next  project but for now the designers and  programmers are busy enjoying the  fantastic success of giana sister's  twisted dreams
 

